The northern and northcentral part of the geographical range of this species overlaps with that of Broscodera chukuai. However, we have not found the two species together (syntopic) (Fig. 50) and our records suggest that they occupy non-overlapping altitudinal ranges and therefore are unlikely to co-occur. Broscodera gaoligongensis appears to be restricted to elevations below 3100 m and mainly well below that level, whereas B. chukuai has been found only at elevations above 3400 m (Fig. 49). The ranges of the other described species do not include Yunnan Province.","","text","",""]]},"MFW6":{"d":[["Southern Asia","","text","",""]]},"ND8V":{"d":[["","AGE","tdwg","",""]]},"NPD3K":{"d":[["Denmark","DK","iso","","not evaluated"]]},"P6NL":{"d":[["","BR","iso","",""]]},"PB6X":{"d":[["Africa","","text","",""]]},"QH3B2":{"d":[["Africa","","text","",""]]},"QJCB":{"d":[["Canary Is.","48087","mrgid","",""]]},"QQTJ":{"d":[["32","32","tdwg","",""]]},"QV7NT":{"d":[["Sweden","SE","iso","native",""]]},"R4LN":{"d":[["China (Sichuan, Yunnan)","","text","",""]]},"R8DR":{"d":[["","AGE","tdwg","",""],["","BOL","tdwg","",""],["","ECU","tdwg","",""],["","MXC","tdwg","",""],["","PER","tdwg","",""]]},"RDL7G":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"RQZRQ":{"d":[["New Zealand Exclusive Economic Zone","8455","mrgid","native",""]]},"RVGQ":{"d":[["Macedonia (Yugoslavia)","","text","native",""]]},"RZL4T":{"d":[["North America","","text","",""]]},"S5GQ":{"d":[["","AFG","tdwg","",""],["","CHT","tdwg","",""],["","NEP","tdwg","",""],["","PAK","tdwg","",""],["","WHM","tdwg","",""]]},"S8RJY":{"d":[["Afrotropic","","text","native",""]]},"S9L4T":{"d":[["Distribution The species is known from Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Italy, The Netherlands, Romania, Spain, Lebanon, Japan, South Africa, Zimbabwe, and USA.","","text","",""]]},"SFVX9":{"d":[["Antipodes Islands","19672","mrgid","native",""],["Auckland Islands","17378","mrgid","native",""],["Campbell Island","14798","mrgid","native",""]]},"SJKC5":{